    "question": "A 2-year-old girl is brought to the physician by her father because she suddenly stopped using her right arm. Earlier in the day, the father lifted her up by the hand to help her over a curb. The child cried briefly and has not moved the arm since. On physical examination, the child holds the arm close to her body with the elbow slightly flexed and the forearm pronated. There is no swelling, bruising, or deformity noted. She resists any attempt to move the elbow. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
