    "question": "A 59-year-old male in the ICU is being monitored following an aortic valve transplant and median sternotomy. He has become acutely septic. Physical examination reveals erythema around the surgical site. Palpation of the area elicits a clicking sound and a crunching sensation, consistent with subcutaneous emphysema. Which of the following best describes the organism responsible for this patient's condition?",
