    "question": "A 56-year-old woman with a significant smoking history presents for evaluation of a persistent cough. She has a history of hypertension managed with lisinopril and dyslipidemia managed with a statin. A pulmonary biopsy is performed, revealing distinct pink, circular structures composed of keratin. Which of the following laboratory findings is most likely to be present in this patient?",
