      "Option D: Incorrect because hyponatremia is typically associated with the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone (SIADH), which is a paraneoplastic syndrome of small cell lung carcinoma, not squamous cell carcinoma.",
      "Option E: Incorrect because increased urinary osmolality is a feature of SIADH (seen in small cell carcinoma), where excessive ADH causes water retention and concentrated urine."
