      "Clinical Reasoning: The presentation of a painless flank mass in a young child is highly suggestive of Wilms tumor. Ultrasound is the preferred initial imaging modality in children to avoid the radiation exposure associated with CT scans. Aniridia, or the absence of the iris, is a classic phenotypic association with the WT1 mutation found in WAGR syndrome.",
