    "question": "A 23-year-old male presents with progressive fatigue and difficulty walking over the past several months. He reports numbness and tingling in his feet and occasional balance issues. He has had an unintentional weight loss of 4 kg over the last 6 months. Physical examination reveals pallor and a smooth, shiny tongue. Neurological exam shows decreased vibratory sensation in the lower extremities and diminished ankle reflexes. He demonstrates a positive Romberg sign. Laboratory studies show an MCV of 104 fL. What is the most likely explanation for this patient's findings?",
