    "question": "An 83-year-old male presents for a routine health maintenance examination. Laboratory studies show a bleeding time of 7 minutes (normal: 2-7 minutes), a partial thromboplastin time (PTT) of 36 seconds (normal: 25-40 seconds), and a prothrombin time (PT) of 13 seconds (normal: 10-15 seconds). His past medical history is unremarkable, and he takes no medications. Physical examination of his right wrist reveals a non-palpable, purpuric lesion. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for the patient's findings?",
    "vitals": null,
