      "Clinical Reasoning: The presentation of recurrent sinopulmonary infections (pneumonia, sinusitis) in a teenager or young adult is highly suggestive of IgA deficiency. The association with atopy (atopic dermatitis) and autoimmune conditions (autoimmune gastritis/pernicious anemia in the brother) are classic clinical clues for this condition.",
