    "question": "A 33-year-old woman presents with a 2-week history of a scaling, ring-shaped lesion on her forearm. She mentions that she frequently attends yoga classes and recently adopted a puppy. Physical examination reveals an annular, erythematous patch with peripheral scaling and central clearing. A diagnosis of Tinea corporis is made, and a topical antifungal agent is prescribed. Which of the following best describes the mechanism of action of the most likely prescribed medication?",
