      "Clinical Reasoning: Ergosterol is an essential component of the fungal cell membrane, serving a similar structural role to cholesterol in human cells. By blocking its synthesis, azoles disrupt the integrity of the fungal cell membrane, leading to cell death. The patient's history of yoga mats and a new puppy are classic 'buzzword' associations for the transmission of dermatophytes.",
