    "question": "A 68-year-old woman presents to the emergency department following a 20-minute episode of numbness in her left leg and sudden confusion. During the episode, she was disoriented to person, place, and time. Her symptoms have since completely resolved. She has a history of hypertension for which she takes hydrochlorothiazide and nifedipine. A non-contrast CT of the head shows no evidence of intracranial hemorrhage. Which of the following brain areas was most likely affected during this episode?",
