    "question": "A 59-year-old male presents with a 7-month history of an intermittent dry cough that has gradually progressed to shortness of breath on exertion and daytime fatigue. He has no significant past medical history. Physical examination reveals dry inspiratory crackles on auscultation. A high-resolution CT of the chest shows a reticular/reticulonodular pattern with honeycombing. Which of the following additional findings is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
