    "question": "A 42-year-old male is evaluated in the hospital. Physical examination reveals velvety, hyperpigmented plaques on the nape of his neck and axillae. Imaging of the chest reveals a large mass in the right lung, suspicious for pulmonary carcinoma. Which of the following is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
