    "question": "A 61-year-old male presents with a 20-minute episode of painless loss of vision in his left eye that resolved spontaneously. He has a 41-pack-year smoking history. His BMI is 24 kg/m\u00b2, blood pressure is 150/90 mmHg, and HbA1c is 5.5%. An ECG shows sinus rhythm at 80 bpm. Which of the following interventions is most likely to reduce the risk of future episodes?",
