    "learning_objective": "The Bottom Line: Meckel diverticulum is a remnant of the vitelline duct that often contains heterotopic gastric mucosa, leading to acid-induced ileal ulceration, occult bleeding, and iron deficiency anemia, diagnosable via a Technetium-99m pertechnetate scan.",
    "source_episode": "HY USMLE Q #1454 \u2013 Gastro",
    "id": "90e04f53"
