    "question": "A 32-year-old woman presents with a history of confusion, fever, and fatigue. She has noticed sudden bruising on her arms and legs along with several scattered petechiae. Physical examination reveals mild scleral icterus and a mild facial droop on the right. Laboratory studies show a hemoglobin of 11 g/dL, platelets of 50,000/mm\u00b3, and increased serum LDH. A peripheral blood smear is shown, revealing schistocytes. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
