    "question": "A 6-year-old boy presents with generalized edema and a positive fluid wave on abdominal examination. Urinalysis reveals significant proteinuria but no hematuria. Light microscopy of a renal biopsy shows no significant changes, but electron microscopy reveals effacement of the podocyte foot processes. Which of the following conditions shares a similar nephrotic presentation without hematuria?",
