    "question": "A 67-year-old woman presents with a dull, aching pain in her right knee. The pain is worse in the evening after a day of activity and improves with rest. She reports some morning stiffness that resolves within 15 minutes. Physical examination reveals bony enlargement of the knee with crepitus and decreased mobility. There is no warmth, erythema, or effusion. Bony nodules are noted on her distal and proximal interphalangeal joints. Which of the following is most likely to have prevented this patient's condition?",
