    "question": "A 66-year-old woman presents for a follow-up appointment regarding her long-standing diabetes mellitus and dyslipidemia. She is currently managed with insulin, enalapril, and atorvastatin. On physical examination, her blood pressure is 130/80 mmHg. Laboratory studies reveal a creatinine of 4.4 mg/dL (normal: 0.7-1.2), BUN of 70 mg/dL (normal: <20), sodium of 140 mEq/L, potassium of 6.1 mEq/L (normal: 3.5-5.0), and calcium of 7.5 mg/dL (normal: 8.4-10.2). Which of the following is most likely seen in this patient?",
