    "question": "A 9-year-old boy presents with a 12-hour history of dark cola-colored urine. His past medical history is unremarkable except for a fever and sore throat two weeks ago, for which he completed a one-week course of penicillin. Physical examination is notable for mild periorbital edema. Which of the following is most likely to be found in this patient?",
