    "question": "A 30-year-old male is evaluated in the hospital. His father has a history of cirrhosis. Arterial blood gas analysis shows a pH of 7.39, bicarbonate of 24 mEq/L, PO2 of 90 mmHg, and PCO2 of 38 mmHg. The total oxygen content in the blood is found to be low. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
