    "question": "A 66-year-old male presents with progressive dyspnea and orthopnea. He reports waking up at night gasping for air and notes that his ankles appear fuller toward the evening. Physical examination reveals pedal edema. A chest X-ray is performed, showing a significantly dilated cardiac silhouette. Which of the following is most likely to be found in this patient?",
