    "question": "A 58-year-old male with a 20-year history of type 2 diabetes mellitus presents with worsening swelling in his lower extremities and fatigue. Physical examination reveals 3+ pitting edema to the knees and a blood pressure of 155/95 mmHg. Laboratory studies show a serum albumin of 2.4 g/dL and 4+ proteinuria on urinalysis. A renal biopsy is performed, showing pink, nodular hyaline deposits within the glomerular mesangium, consistent with Kimmelstiel-Wilson nodules. Which of the following is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
