      "Clinical Reasoning: The absent cremasteric reflex is a highly sensitive finding for testicular torsion. This reflex is mediated by the genitofemoral nerve (L1-L2). The afferent limb is the femoral branch of the genitofemoral nerve (and ilioinguinal nerve), while the efferent limb is the genital branch of the genitofemoral nerve. In torsion, the twisting of the spermatic cord causes impingement of the genital branch, resulting in a negative reflex.",
