    "question": "A 31-year-old male from Massachusetts presents with a 3-day history of yellowing of the eyes, fatigue, and a low-grade fever. He has no significant past medical history and has not traveled outside of the United States recently. Physical examination is notable for scleral icterus. A peripheral blood smear is performed, revealing intraerythrocytic parasites in ring forms and tetrad formations (Maltese cross). Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
