    "question": "A 17-year-old male presents with a 2-day history of sore throat and fever. He has no significant past medical history. Physical examination reveals tonsillar exudates and cervical lymphadenopathy. He reports no cough. His temperature is 102\u00b0F. A rapid strep test is negative, and a throat culture is performed. He is started on empiric amoxicillin. A peripheral blood smear is obtained and shows atypical lymphocytes with abundant, amorphous cytoplasm. Which of the following is most likely to occur in this patient?",
