    "question": "A 27-year-old woman presents with several weeks of shortness of breath, hemoptysis, and persistent headaches. She gave birth to her first child four months ago and has experienced intermittent vaginal spotting since delivery. Physical examination reveals bilateral lung crackles and papilledema. A chest X-ray shows multiple \"cannonball-shaped\" opacities throughout both lung fields. A brain MRI reveals multiple hemorrhagic lesions. Laboratory studies show a significantly elevated beta-hCG level. A pelvic ultrasound demonstrates a heterogeneous intrauterine mass with increased vascularity. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
