    "question": "A 19-year-old woman presents for a routine evaluation. Physical examination reveals short stature, a rounded face (moon facies), and subcutaneous ossifications. On examination of her feet, there is notable shortening of the fourth and fifth metatarsals. Laboratory studies show a serum calcium of 9 mg/dL (normal: 8.4\u201310.2 mg/dL) and a serum phosphate of 3.3 mg/dL (normal: 3.0\u20134.5 mg/dL). Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
