      "Option C: Hypothyroidism is not a classic component of CHARGE syndrome. It is more frequently associated with Down syndrome or congenital iodine deficiency (cretinism).",
      "Option D: Lipomas are soft tissue tumors that, when found in conjunction with familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP), suggest Gardner syndrome.",
      "Option E: Recurrent pneumonia is characteristic of immunodeficiencies (like IgA deficiency) or mucociliary clearance disorders (like Cystic Fibrosis or Kartagener syndrome), but not CHARGE syndrome."
