    "question": "A 34-year-old woman presents with a history of foul-smelling, fatty, floaty stools (steatorrhea) after a recent wilderness trip where she went swimming and scuba diving in a freshwater lake. Microscopic examination of her stool reveals pear-shaped trophozoites with two nuclei and multiple flagella, as well as oval-shaped cysts. Which of the following describes the mechanism of action for the most appropriate pharmacotherapy for this patient?",
