      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient's presentation of steatorrhea (fatty stools) following exposure to freshwater in the wilderness is classic for Giardiasis. The identification of trophozoites and cysts in the stool confirms the diagnosis of Giardia lamblia, a flagellated protozoan.",
      "Key Association: Remember the mnemonic 'GET GAP on the Metro' to recall the coverage of Metronidazole: Giardia, Entamoeba, Trichomonas, Gardnerella, Anaerobes (below the diaphragm), and H. Pylori (second-line)."
