    "question": "A 56-year-old woman presents with dysuria. She has a 20-year history of type 2 diabetes mellitus managed with insulin. Her BMI is 30. Physical examination reveals a temperature of 100.5\u00b0F, decreased pinprick sensation up to the knees, and a small suprapubic enlargement. In addition to urinary catheterization and antibiotics, which of the following medications would be most beneficial for this patient?",
