    "question": "A 4-year-old girl is evaluated for a suspected congenital heart defect. Oxygen tension measurements are obtained from various cardiopulmonary locations. A significant step-up in oxygen saturation is noted between the superior vena cava and the right atrium. Which of the following physical exam findings is most likely to be present in this patient?",
