    "question": "A 15-year-old boy presents for a follow-up examination. Laboratory studies reveal a bleeding time of 8 minutes (normal: 2-7 minutes), a prothrombin time (PT) of 14 seconds (normal: 10-15 seconds), an activated partial thromboplastin time (PTT) of 48 seconds (normal: 25-40 seconds), and a platelet count of 220,000/mm\u00b3 (normal: 150,000-450,000/mm\u00b3). Which of the following is the most likely explanation for the patient's findings?",
