    "question": "A 67-year-old woman presents with a 6-month history of mid-upper back pain and pain in her right humerus. Serum protein electrophoresis (SPEP) is performed, revealing a distinct monoclonal (M) protein spike, specifically identified as a kappa-lambda light chain IgG spike. Bone marrow biopsy is planned to confirm the suspected diagnosis. Which of the following additional findings is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
