    "question": "A 24-year-old woman presents with a 1-year history of inability to conceive. Physical examination and imaging of the uterus demonstrate an external fundal indentation. A hysterosalpingogram is performed, revealing a V-shaped uterine cavity rather than the normal triangular shape. Which of the following embryological processes most likely failed in this patient?",
