      "Clinical Reasoning: The key diagnostic feature mentioned is the 'external fundal indentation.' This is the pathognomonic differentiator between a bicornuate uterus and a septate uterus. In a bicornuate uterus, the failure of fusion creates a 'heart-shaped' external contour. The V-shaped cavity on hysterosalpingogram (HSG) confirms the presence of two distinct uterine horns, which can contribute to infertility or recurrent pregnancy loss.",
