    "question": "A 4-year-old boy presents with recurrent bacterial pneumonia since the age of 6 months. He is at the 5th percentile for weight and height. His mother reports that her brother has a long history of infertility and produced a sample showing no sperm. Physical examination and X-ray reveal bilateral genu varum. Which of the following is the most likely underlying mechanism for this patient's skeletal findings?",
