      "Primary Mechanism: This patient has Cystic Fibrosis (CF), caused by a defect in the CFTR (Cystic Fibrosis Transmembrane Conductance Regulator) protein, which functions as a chloride channel. In the lungs and pancreas, defective CFTR prevents chloride from leaving the cell. To maintain electrical neutrality, the Epithelial Sodium Channel (ENaC) is upregulated, leading to increased sodium and water reabsorption into the cell. This results in thick, dehydrated (inspissated) secretions.",
