    "question": "A 28-year-old woman presents with a 2-day history of a diffuse maculopapular rash. She recently recovered from septic arthritis caused by Staphylococcus aureus, for which she was treated with IV cefazolin in the hospital followed by oral cephalexin as an outpatient. Urinalysis reveals the presence of eosinophils. Which of the following histological findings is most likely present in this patient?",
