    "question": "A 12-year-old boy presents with a 3-month history of increasingly awkward walking and hip pain. Physical examination reveals an antalgic gait. He is 6 feet tall and weighs 190 lbs. An X-ray of the hip is performed and shows an 'ice cream slipping off the cone' appearance of the femoral head. Which of the following is the most likely finding in this patient?",
