    "question": "A patient with a long-standing history of smoking and chronic hypertension is evaluated for cardiovascular risk reduction. The physician notes that the patient's blood pressure is consistently elevated at 180/100 mmHg despite current management. Which of the following interventions is the most effective for specifically reducing this patient's risk of stroke?",
