    "question": "A 39-year-old woman presents with a one-week history of epistaxis. She has no significant past medical history. Laboratory studies show a hemoglobin of 11 g/dL, leukocytes of 5,000/mm\u00b3, and a platelet count of 40,000/mm\u00b3. Prothrombin time (PT) is 12 seconds, and partial thromboplastin time (PTT) is 27 seconds. Bleeding time is elevated at 9 minutes. A peripheral blood smear shows pale red blood cells and a marked decrease in platelets. What is the next best step in management?",
