    "question": "A 67-year-old man is brought to the emergency department by ambulance. He is found to be hypotensive with a blood pressure of 90/60 mmHg, tachycardic at 112/min, and tachypneic at 20/min. An arterial pressure tracing is obtained, which demonstrates a decrease in systolic blood pressure of 12 mmHg during inspiration. Which of the following findings is most likely to be seen on this patient's electrocardiogram?",
