    "question": "A 64-year-old male presents with symptoms of left heart failure, evidenced by pulmonary edema and cephalization of pulmonary vessels on imaging. He has a history of dyslipidemia and hypertension but does not have diabetes and is a non-smoker. Physical examination reveals bibasilar crackles. Echocardiography confirms a reduced ejection fraction. What is the most appropriate next step in the management of this patient?",
