      "Clinical Reasoning: IE prophylaxis for dental procedures is reserved for high-risk groups: those with prosthetic heart valves (including transcatheter-implanted valves), a prior history of infective endocarditis, or specific types of congenital heart disease (unrepaired cyanotic heart disease or repaired disease with prosthetic material). Since this patient only has native valvular regurgitation, antibiotics are not indicated.",
