      "Clinical Reasoning: The location (approximately 2 feet or 60 cm from the ileocecal valve) and the presence of an outpouching on imaging are classic for Meckel's. While often associated with the 'Rule of 2s' (2% of the population, 2 inches long, 2 feet from the ileocecal valve, 2 types of heterotopic tissue, presenting by age 2), it can certainly present in older children and young adults, as seen in this 18-year-old patient.",
