    "question": "A 40-year-old male presents with a 5-month history of a dry cough and redness of both shins. A biopsy of a skin lesion is performed, revealing collections of multinucleated coalesced macrophages and epithelioid activated histiocytes. Which of the following is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
