    "question": "A 54-year-old male with a history of obesity and sedentary lifestyle presents for a routine check-up. Laboratory studies reveal a fasting blood glucose of 145 mg/dL and an HbA1c of 8.2%. He is diagnosed with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. In this patient's current metabolic state, which of the following best describes the activity of glycerol kinase, hormone-sensitive lipase (HSL), and glucokinase compared to a healthy individual in the fed state?",
