      "Clinical Reasoning: Hormone-sensitive lipase (HSL) is responsible for mobilizing fatty acids from adipose tissue into the bloodstream. In the absence of effective insulin signaling (insulin normally inhibits HSL), HSL activity increases, leading to elevated free fatty acids. Conversely, glucokinase (the liver's hexokinase variant) is induced by insulin to facilitate glycolysis and glycogen synthesis. In insulin resistance, glucokinase activity is significantly decreased, further contributing to hyperglycemia.",
