    "question": "A 6-month-old boy is brought to the pediatrician by his mother, who is concerned about his aggressive behavior and recent episodes of self-mutilation, specifically biting his lips and fingers. During the examination, the mother notes the presence of red-orange, sand-like crystals in the patient's diaper. Laboratory analysis reveals a deficiency in hypoxanthine-guanine phosphoribosyltransferase (HGPRT). Which of the following conditions shares the same inheritance pattern as this patient's diagnosis?",
    "vitals": null,
