    "question": "A 26-year-old woman and her 28-year-old husband present to a genetic counselor to discuss the risk of their future children inheriting cystic fibrosis (CF). The woman is phenotypically normal but has a younger brother who was diagnosed with CF shortly after birth. The husband has no family history of the disease. The prevalence of cystic fibrosis in the general population is approximately 1 in 40,000. What is the probability that this couple will have a daughter affected by cystic fibrosis?",
    "vitals": null,
