    "question": "A 2-week-old newborn male presents with ambiguous genitalia. Physical examination reveals a 2 cm phallus and partially fused labioscrotal folds. Karyotype is confirmed as 46, XX. Imaging shows no uterus. Serum testosterone levels are normal for a newborn. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
