      "Clinical Reasoning: The pathognomonic finding in this case is the 'blue dot sign,' which represents the infarcted, cyanotic appendix testis visible through the thin scrotal skin. Furthermore, the presence of an intact cremasteric reflex (testicular retraction upon inner thigh stimulation) is a critical finding that helps rule out testicular torsion.",
