      "Primary Mechanism: In the evaluation of malignancies like transitional cell carcinoma (TCC) of the bladder, tumor stage (TNM classification) is the most significant predictor of prognosis. Stage describes the anatomical extent of the tumor, including the depth of invasion (T), lymph node involvement (N), and distant metastasis (M). Grade, on the other hand, describes the degree of cellular differentiation and mitotic activity (atypia).",
