    "question": "A 10-year-old boy presents with dark-colored urine and facial puffiness that began five days ago. Three weeks prior, he was prescribed topical mupirocin for several honey-crusted lesions on his arms. Physical examination reveals periorbital edema and 1+ mild bilateral lower extremity swelling. Urinalysis shows 3+ blood and 2+ protein. Which of the following is the most likely finding on renal biopsy for this patient?",
