      "Clinical Reasoning: Gq protein activation normally stimulates phospholipase C, which cleaves PIP2 into inositol trisphosphate (IP3) and diacylglycerol (DAG). By irreversibly blocking the alpha-1 receptor, phenoxybenzamine prevents the binding of catecholamines, thereby inhibiting the Gq pathway and leading to decreased levels of IP3 and DAG.",
      "Key Association: Use the mnemonic 'Have 1 or 3 M&Ms' to remember Gq-coupled receptors: H1, Alpha-1, V1, M1, and M3. Since alpha-1 is Gq, blocking it reduces the downstream second messengers IP3 and DAG."
