      "Option D: Decreased cAMP is associated with Gi-coupled receptors (M2, Alpha-2, D2). While phenoxybenzamine blocks alpha-2 receptors (which would actually increase cAMP by preventing Gi-mediated inhibition), its primary therapeutic effect in pheochromocytoma is the blockade of alpha-1 mediated vasoconstriction."
