    "question": "A 68-year-old male with a history of heavy smoking presents with a 2-week history of progressive confusion and lethargy. He was recently diagnosed with a mass in the right upper lobe of his lung. Laboratory studies show a serum sodium of 122 mEq/L (Normal: 135-145 mEq/L) and a urine osmolality of 550 mOsm/kg (Normal: 50-1200 mOsm/kg). Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
