    "question": "A 3-week-old male newborn born at term presents with jaundice. The pregnancy and delivery were uncomplicated. He is breastfeeding, though the mother reports some difficulty with him attaching to the breast at times. Laboratory studies show a total bilirubin of 13 mg/dL, a direct bilirubin of 10 mg/dL, and a hemoglobin of 15 g/dL. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for this patient's presentation?",
