    "question": "A 32-year-old female presents with a several-month history of weight gain, cold intolerance, and persistent constipation. She also notes that her menstrual cycles have become irregular. Physical examination reveals a diffuse, non-tender enlargement of the thyroid gland. Laboratory evaluation shows an elevated TSH, decreased free T4, and positive anti-thyroperoxidase (anti-microsomal) antibodies. A biopsy of the thyroid gland is performed. Which of the following histological findings is most likely?",
