    "question": "A 3-year-old boy is brought to the clinic for recurrent skin and pulmonary infections. Physical examination reveals silvery hair, nystagmus, and hepatosplenomegaly. The patient's skin is notably fairer than his 6-year-old sister's. Laboratory analysis of a peripheral blood smear shows neutrophils containing giant granules. Which of the following is the most likely underlying mechanism of this patient's condition?",
