      "Primary Mechanism: Severe Combined Immunodeficiency (SCID) can be caused by an autosomal recessive deficiency in Adenosine Deaminase (ADA). ADA is required for the degradation of adenosine and deoxyadenosine; its absence leads to the accumulation of dATP, which is toxic to both B and T lymphocytes.",
