    "question": "A 4-year-old boy has a history of recurrent lymphadenitis and skin abscesses. Cultures have previously grown Staphylococcus aureus, Serratia marcescens, and Aspergillus. A nitroblue tetrazolium (NBT) test is performed and fails to turn blue. What is the defective enzyme in this patient?",
