    "question": "A 38-year-old woman presents with a two-week history of hematuria and fatigue. She reports coughing up a small amount of blood one week ago, which she initially attributed to a sore throat. Laboratory studies are positive for antiproteinase 3 (PR3) antibodies. A renal biopsy is performed, revealing crescentic glomerulonephritis. Which of the following is most likely to be associated with this patient's condition?",
