    "question": "A 33-year-old G3P2 woman at 34 weeks gestation is brought to the emergency department with a 2-hour history of vaginal bleeding. She reports no abdominal pain, contractions, or recent trauma. Fetal movements have been normal. She has received regular prenatal care with no prior complications. Physical examination shows no uterine tenderness. Fetal heart rate is 145/min. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
