    "question": "A 62-year-old male presents with a 3-month history of progressively worsening shortness of breath on exertion. Physical examination reveals peripheral edema, jugular venous distension, and hepatomegaly. An S4 heart sound is auscultated. Transthoracic echocardiography shows concentric left ventricular hypertrophy and an ejection fraction of 60%. A biopsy of the myocardium is performed, showing lighter eosinophilic areas mixed with darker eosinophilic areas. Which of the following is the most likely cause of the patient's condition?",
