    "question": "A 41-year-old woman presents with a 2-day history of blisters on her lips and cheeks. Her medical history is significant for type 1 diabetes mellitus, for which she takes insulin and enalapril. One week ago, she was diagnosed with Mycoplasma pneumonia and treated with a course of antibiotics. A chest X-ray at that time revealed bilateral interstitial infiltrates. Which of the following mechanisms of action is most likely responsible for the patient's current skin findings?",
