    "question": "A 65-year-old male is brought to the hospital by his family due to recent onset of visual hallucinations and confusion. His family also notes that he has been having frequent, watery bowel movements over the past week. Physical examination reveals hyperpigmentation and scaling of the skin on his forearms and a distinct hyperpigmented rash around his neck. Which of the following is most likely associated with the underlying cause of this patient's condition?",
