    "question": "A 30-year-old female presents with symptoms consistent with pyelonephritis, including costovertebral angle (CVA) tenderness. Her temperature is 103\u00b0F, blood pressure is 120/80 mmHg, and her leukocyte count is 23,000/mm\u00b3. She is started on daily IV ceftriaxone for community-acquired sepsis. Despite 72 hours of appropriate antibiotic therapy, the patient remains febrile. Which of the following is the next best step in management?",
