      "Clinical Reasoning: Random mode introduces 'shock value' when a student encounters a topic they haven't seen in weeks. Getting a question wrong under these circumstances creates a more durable memory trace compared to getting it right during a concentrated subject block. The 'tutor' aspect allows for immediate feedback, which is essential for correcting misconceptions in real-time.",
