    "question": "A neonatal male born at 37 weeks gestation via spontaneous vaginal delivery presents with immediate respiratory distress and cyanosis. Physical examination reveals reduced breath sounds on the left side of the chest, and heart sounds are auscultated most loudly on the right side. The abdomen appears scaphoid with absent bowel sounds. A chest X-ray shows bowel loops in the left hemithorax and a mediastinal shift to the right. An orogastric tube is inserted and is subsequently observed in the left hemithorax on a repeat X-ray. What is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
