    "question": "A 4-year-old boy is brought to the clinic by his mother due to progressive difficulty standing up from a seated position. Physical examination reveals weakening of the pelvic girdle muscles and apparent enlargement of the calves. When asked to stand from the floor, the boy uses his hands to 'walk up' his legs. Which of the following best describes the inheritance pattern, the most likely type of mutation, and the cellular classification of this disorder?",
