    "question": "A 30-year-old woman presents with a one-week history of worsening urinary incontinence, characterized by an urgent need to run to the bathroom 8 to 12 times daily. She reports a similar episode three years ago that was successfully treated with oxybutynin. Physical examination is notable for a positive Babinski sign on the left and clonus of the right hand. Which of the following is most likely to be part of this patient's acute presentation?",
