    "question": "A 43-year-old male with a history of Hepatitis C and HIV presents with a 4-day history of severe neck pain and fever. He is a known intravenous drug user. On physical examination, his temperature is 103\u00b0F. Cardiac auscultation reveals a 3/6 holosystolic murmur loudest at the apex. His neck is tender over the cervical spine, but there is no associated warmth or erythema. Neurological examination is normal. A chest X-ray is unremarkable, but a cervical spine X-ray shows destructive alterations in the C4 through C6 vertebrae. What is the most likely mechanism of this patient's neck pain?",
