    "question": "A 28-year-old woman presents with a 4-month history of fatigue. Laboratory studies show a hemoglobin of 11 g/dL, an MCV of 70 fL, and elevated levels of hemoglobin A2 and hemoglobin F. Prothrombin time (PT) is 13 seconds and partial thromboplastin time (PTT) is 37 seconds. Which of the following is the most likely underlying cause of this patient's condition?",
