    "question": "A 9-year-old boy presents with a 1-month history of fatigue. He has no recent illnesses or significant past medical history. Physical examination is notable for mild scleral icterus and a palpable spleen tip. Laboratory studies reveal a mild normochromic, normocytic anemia with an increased mean corpuscular hemoglobin concentration (MCHC). An eosin-5-maleimide (EMA) binding test is positive. The patient's father has a history of both splenectomy and cholecystectomy. Which of the following is the most likely underlying genetic or molecular defect in this patient?",
