    "question": "A 6-week-old boy is brought to the pediatrician by his mother for a 2-week history of gradual enlargement of the left scrotum. On physical examination, the left hemiscrotum is enlarged and non-tender. Transillumination of the left hemiscrotum reveals a clear, fluid-filled sac. The remainder of the physical exam is unremarkable. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management and the underlying mechanism of this condition?",
