    "question": "A 40-year-old woman presents to her physician with poor concentration, feelings of guilt, and suicidal thoughts. She cannot recall when her symptoms began. Her mother and brother have had similar symptoms. She also reports intermittent abdominal pain and notes that she avoids alcohol because it triggers these episodes. Physical examination is unremarkable except for a positive Romberg sign. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for this patient's findings?",
