      "Option B: Multiple Sclerosis (MS) is an inflammatory demyelinating disease of the CNS. While it can cause a positive Romberg sign and psychiatric symptoms, it typically presents with optic neuritis, internuclear ophthalmoplegia (MLF syndrome), or upper motor neuron signs. It lacks the characteristic abdominal pain and clear autosomal dominant family history.",
