    "question": "A 30-year-old male presents with a 2-month history of a progressive, mildly itchy rash on his back. Physical examination reveals well-demarcated erythematous plaques with an overlying silvery scale. VDRL testing is negative. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
