      "Option D: Secondary syphilis presents with a diffuse maculopapular rash that frequently involves the palms and soles. It would typically be associated with a positive VDRL or RPR screen.",
      "Option E: Tinea corporis (ringworm) presents as annular, erythematous patches with central clearing and a scaly border. It is a fungal infection often linked to contact with pets or contaminated surfaces.",
