    "question": "A 74-year-old male is admitted to the emergency department with a 24-hour history of hematochezia (bright red blood per rectum). His medical history is significant for COPD and ischemic heart disease. Current medications include lisinopril, metoprolol, aspirin, and simvastatin. On physical examination, he is afebrile, his pulse is 90/min, and his blood pressure is 135/90 mmHg. The abdominal examination is unremarkable, but a rectal examination reveals clots and dark blood. The bleeding resolves spontaneously four hours after admission. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
