    "question": "A 30-year-old woman is brought to the emergency department due to gradual diminished vision in her left eye that began six hours ago. She reports a mild headache over the left eye that started before she went to sleep last night. Funduscopic examination shows no abnormalities; however, she is unable to read text or count fingers with her left eye. Visual acuity is normal in the right eye. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
