    "question": "A 42-year-old male presents with a 6-month history of progressively worsening visual loss and left hip pain. Physical examination reveals diminished peripheral vision bilaterally. An X-ray of the hip shows a contracted femoral head. The patient also reports a 10-pound weight gain over the same period. Which of the following hormones is most likely responsible for this patient's condition?",
