    "question": "A 46-year-old woman presents with painful blisters on her skin and within her oral cavity. Physical examination reveals multiple flaccid bullae and a positive Nikolsky sign, characterized by the sloughing of the epidermis when lateral pressure is applied to the skin. Which of the following cellular structures is the primary target of the autoantibodies in this patient's condition?",
