      "Clinical Reasoning: The increased systemic absorption of oxalate leads to hyperoxaluria. Once filtered by the kidneys, the oxalate combines with urinary calcium to form calcium oxalate stones. This is a classic complication of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) involving the small bowel.",
