    "question": "An 84-year-old male presents with a 2-day history of severe generalized abdominal pain. He has a long-standing history of type 2 diabetes mellitus managed with insulin. On physical examination, there is mild diffuse tenderness to palpation. Laboratory studies show a sodium of 140 mEq/L, potassium of 4.2 mEq/L, and bicarbonate of 20 mEq/L. A CT scan of the abdomen reveals thickening of the small bowel wall. Which of the following is the next best step in management?",
