      "Option B: Dopamine may be used in specific cases of cardiogenic shock (often seen in pediatric board questions with cardiomegaly), but it has no role in the primary management of mesenteric ischemia.",
      "Option C: Heparin is indicated for acute limb ischemia (e.g., embolic events from atrial fibrillation) or vertebral artery dissection, but it is not the definitive diagnostic step for mesenteric ischemia.",
      "Option E: While operative management (laparotomy/celiotomy) is the definitive treatment for bowel necrosis, mesenteric angiography is the preferred diagnostic step to confirm the diagnosis and map the vasculature in a hemodynamically stable patient."
