    "question": "A 40-year-old male with a history of hypertension managed with hydrochlorothiazide presents for a routine follow-up. His vitals are within normal limits. A peripheral blood smear is performed and reveals pale red blood cells with increased central pallor. Which of the following laboratory findings is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
