    "question": "A 68-year-old male presents to the emergency department with crushing substernal chest pain and diaphoresis. He is diagnosed with an acute myocardial infarction. Physical examination reveals a blood pressure of 85/50 mmHg and a heart rate of 110 bpm. An electrocardiogram (ECG) is performed, showing ST-segment elevations in leads II, III, and aVF. Which of the following best describes the most likely acid-base disturbance and the coronary vessel involved in this patient's condition?",
