      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient's presentation of hypertension, bilateral renal enlargements on ultrasound, and a polycystin mutation is diagnostic of ADPKD. ADPKD typically presents in the 30s to 40s. The question asks for another condition with an autosomal dominant inheritance pattern. Hereditary Spherocytosis is the only option provided that follows this pattern.",
