    "question": "An 80-year-old male presents with an inability to void and urinary incontinence. His medical history is significant for seasonal allergies, benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), hypertension, and left heart failure. His current medications include chlorpheniramine, metoprolol, lisinopril, atorvastatin, and terazosin. He was also recently prescribed metoclopramide for an episode of indigestion. Physical examination reveals normal vital signs, but a post-void residual volume is measured at 400 mL (normal < 50-75 mL). Which of the following medications is the most likely cause of this patient's urinary retention?",
    "vitals": null,
