      "Option B: Pyruvate kinase deficiency is the second most common enzyme deficiency causing hemolysis. It results in decreased ATP production, leading to rigid RBCs and extravascular hemolysis, but it is less classically associated with the specific family history of early cholecystectomy seen in HS.",
