    "learning_objective": "The Bottom Line: Hereditary spherocytosis is an autosomal dominant defect in RBC cytoskeletal proteins (ankyrin, spectrin) that presents with normocytic anemia, spherocytes, and increased osmotic fragility; it is frequently associated with pigment gallstones and splenomegaly.",
    "source_episode": "HY USMLE Q #1112 \u2013 Hematology",
