    "question": "A 4-year-old boy is brought to the clinic with a sudden onset of high fever, sore throat, and difficulty swallowing. He is an immigrant and his vaccination status is unknown. On examination, he is drooling and sitting in a 'tripod' position. Lateral neck X-ray reveals a 'thumbprint sign,' confirming a diagnosis of epiglottitis caused by Haemophilus influenzae type B. Which of the following best describes the type of vaccine used to prevent this condition?",
