    "question": "A 65-year-old male with a history of chronic kidney disease presents for a routine follow-up. His baseline creatinine is typically between 0.7 and 1.2 mg/dL, but today it is significantly elevated. Which of the following sets of laboratory values is most consistent with his current clinical state of renal failure?",
