      "Option B: Fasciculations are a hallmark of lower motor neuron (LMN) lesions. MS is a disease of the CNS and typically presents with upper motor neuron (UMN) findings.",
      "Option C: Impaired oculomotor nerve (CN III) activity would result in a 'down and out' eye position and impaired convergence. Since convergence is normal in this patient, CN III is intact.",
      "Option D: T-cell infiltration within the endomysium is the characteristic histopathological finding for polymyositis, an inflammatory myopathy, not a demyelinating CNS disease."
