    "question": "A 24-year-old male is brought to the emergency department with sudden-onset shortness of breath and audible wheezing. He has a history of asthma but has not used his inhaler in several months. On physical examination, he is using accessory muscles for respiration and has diffuse expiratory wheezing. An arterial blood gas (ABG) is performed prior to any medical intervention. Which of the following sets of findings for partial pressure of carbon dioxide (PCO2) and bicarbonate (HCO3-) is most likely in this patient?",
