    "question": "A 28-year-old male is brought to the emergency department after a motor vehicle accident. Physical examination reveals an inability to extend his wrist and fingers on the right side. The patient's right arm is held in a pronated position, and there is a noticeable decrease in triceps strength. An X-ray of the right upper extremity is most likely to show a fracture at which of the following locations?",
