      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient's presentation of 'wrist drop' (failure of wrist extension) and inability to extend the fingers directly points to radial nerve palsy. The pronated position of the arm suggests supinator involvement, and the decreased triceps function indicates the lesion is proximal enough to affect the branches to the triceps, which is consistent with a midshaft humeral fracture.",
