    "question": "A 9-year-old boy presents with a 2-day history of left hip and knee pain. He recently recovered from an upper respiratory tract viral infection. He has no significant past medical history. On physical examination, he is able to bear weight on the left leg. There is no erythema or warmth over the left hip, though mild tenderness is noted upon palpation. His BMI is 23. Laboratory results show a white blood cell count of 9,000/mm\u00b3 (normal: 4,000\u201311,000/mm\u00b3). Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
