    "question": "A 28-year-old male presents with a one-year history of inability to conceive with his wife. His wife has two children from a previous partner. The patient's medical history is significant for sporadic bacterial pneumonias that were successfully treated with antibiotics. He is a non-smoker and non-drinker. His BMI is 25. Physical examination and vitals are within normal limits. A chest X-ray is performed and reveals the cardiac silhouette is located on the right side of the chest. Which of the following is the most likely underlying mechanism for this patient's condition?",
