      "Clinical Reasoning: The clinical triad of Kartagener syndrome includes situs inversus (evidenced by dextrocardia on X-ray), chronic sinusitis/bronchiectasis (recurrent pneumonias), and infertility. In males, infertility occurs because the sperm flagella are immotile, although sperm are present in the ejaculate. In females, it can lead to ectopic pregnancies due to impaired ciliary action in the fallopian tubes.",
