      "Option B: While tubulin inhibition (colchicine) is correct, NF-\u03baB inhibition (steroids) is not the first-line pairing with colchicine for acute pericarditis; steroids are reserved for refractory cases.",
      "Option C: Prostaglandin synthesis inhibition (NSAIDs) is correct, but xanthine oxidase inhibition (e.g., allopurinol) is used for chronic gout management, not pericarditis. While both gout and pericarditis can be treated with colchicine, the underlying inflammatory processes differ.",
