    "question": "A 25-year-old male presents for evaluation of chronic abdominal pain and bloody diarrhea. A barium enema is performed, revealing a \"lead pipe\" appearance of the colon with a significant loss of haustral markings. Laboratory studies are notable for an elevated p-ANCA. Which of the following additional findings is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
