    "question": "A 51-year-old woman presents with reddish-violaceous papules on her knuckles and a rash across her shoulders. She reports progressive difficulty climbing stairs and rising from a chair. Physical examination reveals Gottron papules and a shawl rash. Laboratory studies show an elevated creatine kinase level. Which of the following is this patient at the greatest increased risk for?",
