      "Clinical Reasoning: The key clinical clue is the timing of the hematuria (dark urine). IgA nephropathy typically presents as 'synpharyngitic' hematuria, occurring within 1 to 3 days of an upper respiratory tract infection (URI). This contrasts with post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis (PSGN), which occurs 1 to 3 weeks after an infection.",
