    "question": "A 25-year-old male presents with polyuria and polydipsia. He recently suffered a gunshot wound to the head. Laboratory studies show a serum osmolality of 310 mOsm/kg, a urine osmolality of 150 mOsm/kg, and a fasting glucose of 85 mg/dL. Following the administration of desmopressin, his urine osmolality increases to 250 mOsm/kg. Which of the following is the most likely underlying cause of this patient's condition?",
