    "question": "A 34-year-old male presents for a routine check-up. Laboratory studies reveal a serum sodium of 140 mEq/L (Normal: 135-145), potassium of 3.3 mEq/L (Normal: 3.5-5.0), and bicarbonate of 29 mEq/L (Normal: 22-28). Further testing shows a high plasma renin level. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
