    "question": "A 47-year-old male presents with a 2-month history of progressively worsening back pain, leg weakness, and difficulty walking. Physical examination reveals decreased muscle strength in the lower extremities bilaterally and a positive Babinski sign on the left. Sensation is reduced in a band-like distribution across the thoracic region. An MRI of the spine shows a well-circumscribed thoracic spinal mass. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
