    "question": "A 50-year-old woman presents for a routine check-up. Laboratory studies reveal a serum calcium of 8.2 mg/dL (normal: 8.4-10.2), a serum phosphate of 5.0 mg/dL (normal: 3.0-4.5), and a serum bicarbonate of 21 mEq/L (normal: 22-28). Which of the following is most likely associated with this patient's condition?",
