    "question": "A 41-year-old woman with a long-standing history of dermatomyositis presents for a follow-up visit. She was started on a course of prednisone therapy two weeks ago due to an acute disease flare-up. This marks her third course of prednisone within the last 18 months. She currently feels well and reports no other symptoms. Her only other medication is a daily oral multivitamin. She is a non-smoker and non-drinker with a BMI of 24. Physical examination reveals mechanic's hands and Gottron papules on the knuckles. Vitals are within normal limits. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in the pharmacologic management of this patient?",
