    "question": "A 59-year-old woman presents with a 6-month history of intermittent abdominal pain and yellowing of the eyes. She has a 40-pack-year smoking history and consumes whiskey periodically. Physical examination is notable for scleral icterus. A Sudan black stain of the stool is negative. Laboratory studies show a total bilirubin of 3 mg/dL, alkaline phosphatase (ALP) of 300 U/L, and an elevated amylase level. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
