    "question": "A 56-year-old woman with a long-standing history of symmetric metacarpal and knee pain presents to the clinic. She is currently taking diclofenac, esomeprazole, methotrexate, and prednisone. On physical examination, she is noted to be bent over at the waist. A chest X-ray reveals bilateral reticulonodular patterning. Which of the following is most likely to be found in this patient's clinical history or diagnostic workup?",
