      "Option D: The reticulonodular pattern on chest X-ray suggests interstitial lung disease (pulmonary fibrosis), which is a restrictive lung disease. Restrictive diseases typically present with a normal or increased FEV1/FVC ratio, whereas a reduced ratio is characteristic of obstructive diseases like COPD or asthma."
