    "question": "A 50-year-old man presents with an enlarging periumbilical mass. Histological examination of the mass reveals a 'starry sky' appearance, characterized by a background of basophilic B cells and interspersed tingible body macrophages. Genetic analysis confirms an 8;14 translocation. Which of the following best describes the function of the gene product involved in this translocation?",
