    "question": "A 33-year-old female presents with a distressing, irresistible urge to move her legs, which worsens in the evening and is partially relieved by walking. She works in a textile factory and reports a normal diet, though she admits to consuming several trays of ice pops daily. Physical examination is unremarkable. What is the most appropriate next step in management?",
