    "question": "A 60-year-old man presents with worsening pain in his right distal femur. Radiographic imaging reveals a Codman triangle and a sunburst appearance of the bone. Physical examination is notable for a heart rate of 110 bpm and the presence of both S3 and S4 heart sounds. Echocardiography demonstrates an ejection fraction of 72%. Which of the following additional findings is most likely to be present in this patient?",
