    "question": "A 28-year-old woman presents with a dry cough and low-grade fever. She is otherwise healthy and active, frequently hiking and rock climbing. A chest X-ray reveals bilateral interstitial infiltrates. Laboratory studies show a white blood cell count of 8,000/mm\u00b3, a hemoglobin level of 9.5 g/dL, and an increased serum lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) level. Which of the following is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
