      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient's clinical picture of atypical pneumonia (dry cough, low-grade fever, interstitial infiltrates) combined with laboratory evidence of hemolysis (anemia with elevated LDH) points toward cold autoimmune hemolytic anemia (AIHA). The direct antiglobulin test (Coombs test) detects these antibodies or complement proteins attached to the surface of red blood cells, confirming an autoimmune process.",
      "Key Association: Mycoplasma pneumoniae is the 'buzzword' organism for walking pneumonia and cold-induced hemolytic anemia mediated by IgM."
