    "question": "A 24-year-old male presents with a one-day history of severe right upper quadrant pain and a temperature of 102\u00b0F. He was recently diagnosed with a hematologic disorder characterized by positive osmotic fragility and eosin-5-maleimide flow cytometry. Laboratory studies show a hemoglobin of 10 g/dL. He is scheduled for a concurrent splenectomy and cholecystectomy. An ultrasound of the abdomen is equivocal, but a HIDA scan shows non-visualization of the gallbladder. What is the most likely underlying etiology of this patient's current acute presentation?",
