    "question": "A 44-year-old woman presents with a 12-hour history of a swollen and painful left thigh. A duplex ultrasound confirms a deep vein thrombosis (DVT). Physical examination reveals edema of the infraorbital region of the face, presacral edema of the lower back, and moderate bilateral pedal edema. Which of the following is most likely associated with this patient's condition?",
