      "Option B: Inhibition of presynaptic SNARE proteins is the mechanism for Botulinum toxin (prevents ACh release, causing flaccid paralysis) and Tetanus toxin (prevents GABA/Glycine release, causing spastic paralysis).",
      "Option D: A poly-D-glutamic acid capsule is a unique virulence factor of Bacillus anthracis, helping it evade phagocytosis; it is not a toxin mechanism that causes HUS.",
      "Option E: Production of phospholipase (specifically alpha toxin/lecithinase) is characteristic of Clostridium perfringens, which causes gas gangrene (myonecrosis) by degrading cell membranes."
