    "question": "A 39-year-old G2P2 woman delivered a healthy newborn at term one week ago. Her first pregnancy was complicated by Group B Streptococcus (GBS) colonization, for which she received intrapartum intravenous ampicillin. During her current pregnancy, her GBS status was unknown. Her temperature during delivery was 37.4\u00b0C (99.3\u00b0F), and rupture of membranes occurred 15 hours prior to delivery. The newborn is now irritable and febrile. A laboratory report from the neonate's blood culture reveals gram-positive rods. Which of the following is the most likely cause of the neonate's condition?",
