    "question": "A 12-year-old boy presents with right knee pain that has persisted for two months. He reports no history of trauma. The pain is exacerbated by physical activity and shows minimal improvement with ibuprofen. There is no family history of musculoskeletal or autoimmune diseases. On physical examination, the patient exhibits an antalgic gait. His BMI is 23. An X-ray of the hip is performed, revealing a displacement of the femoral head epiphysis, often described as 'ice cream falling off the cone.' Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
