      "Clinical Reasoning: Although SCFE is classically associated with obesity, it can occur in children with a normal BMI. A critical diagnostic clue is that hip pathology in children frequently presents as referred knee pain. The antalgic gait and the specific X-ray finding of the epiphysis slipping off the metaphysis confirm the diagnosis.",
