    "question": "A 60-year-old woman presents with an 8-month history of shortness of breath on exertion and a non-productive cough. She has no significant past medical history and takes no medications. She is a non-smoker and works as a lawyer. Pulmonary function testing reveals a forced vital capacity (FVC) of 46% of predicted. A chest X-ray shows fine linear opacities bilaterally. A CT scan of the chest demonstrates a reticulonodular pattern with honeycombing. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
