    "question": "A 35-year-old woman presents with a 24-hour history of headache, fever, and vomiting. Her temperature is 103\u00b0F (39.4\u00b0C). Physical examination reveals weakness of the left upper extremity and nystagmus. Optic fundi cannot be visualized during the ophthalmoscopic exam. Kernig and Brudzinski signs are positive. Which of the following is the next best step in diagnosis?",
