    "question": "A 49-year-old woman presents with a 2-month history of swelling in her right foot. She reports no history of trauma, fever, or pain. She has a 30-year history of type 1 diabetes mellitus. Physical examination reveals swelling of the right forefoot without overt ulcerations. There is decreased sensation of touch, proprioception, and pain below the ankles bilaterally. An X-ray of the ankle shows disorganization and disruption of the tarsometatarsal joints. Which of the following is the most likely cause of these findings?",
