    "question": "A 60-year-old woman undergoes angiography of the right femoral artery for peripheral vascular disease. One week later, a continuous machinery-like murmur is noted at the angiography site. Vitals are as follows: temperature 98.6\u00b0F, heart rate 100/min, respiratory rate 12/min, and blood pressure 130/90 mmHg. Which of the following is most likely to develop in this patient?",
