      "Option B: Primary ciliary dyskinesia (Kartagener syndrome) presents with recurrent respiratory infections similar to CF, but it is typically associated with situs inversus (e.g., dextrocardia), which is not present here.",
      "Option C: Pulmonary edema is a sign of left-sided heart failure (increased pulmonary capillary wedge pressure). This patient presents with signs of right-sided heart failure (peripheral edema, hepatomegaly) secondary to lung disease.",
      "Option E: Rupture of subapical blebs is the classic cause of spontaneous pneumothorax, typically seen in tall, thin young men. It presents with sudden-onset pleuritic chest pain and dyspnea, not chronic signs of heart failure."
