    "question": "A 9-year-old boy presents with a 5-day history of bloody diarrhea and fatigue for the past 3 days. On physical examination, he is afebrile but appears pale with scleral icterus. Laboratory studies show a hemoglobin of 7 g/dL, an MCV of 85 fL, a leukocyte count of 19,000/mm\u00b3, and a platelet count of 60,000/mm\u00b3. A Coombs test is negative. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
