      "Option B: Adrenal cortical hyposecretion (Addison's disease) causes hyperpigmentation due to increased ACTH/MSH production and fatigue. However, it typically presents with hypotension, hyponatremia, and hyperkalemia, and would not cause hepatomegaly or diabetes.",
