    "question": "A 19-year-old woman presents with a 6-month history of joint pain in her knees and hips. She has no significant past medical history. Physical examination reveals a temperature of 100\u00b0F and warmth and swelling of the knees. Laboratory studies show a hemoglobin of 10 g/dL, platelets of 120,000/mm\u00b3, blood urea nitrogen (BUN) of 38 mg/dL, and creatinine of 1.7 mg/dL. Urinalysis reveals 1+ blood and 1+ protein. Which of the following is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
