      "Clinical Reasoning: The presence of a 'dendritic' or tree-like pattern on fluorescein staining is the classic diagnostic finding for keratitis caused by Herpes Simplex Virus (HSV-1 or HSV-2) or Varicella-Zoster Virus (VZV). The clinical presentation of blurred vision and mild ocular pain in the setting of these findings confirms the diagnosis of viral keratitis.",
