      "Option B: 50S ribosomal subunit inhibitors include macrolides (e.g., azithromycin), clindamycin, and linezolid. These are antibacterial agents and are not indicated for viral keratitis.",
      "Option D: RNA polymerase inhibition is the mechanism of action for rifampin (specifically DNA-dependent RNA polymerase). Rifampin is primarily used in the treatment of tuberculosis and prophylaxis for meningococcal or H. influenzae type b meningitis."
