      "Option D: Gastric emptying scintigraphy is the gold-standard confirmatory test for gastroparesis, showing delayed emptying of a radiolabeled meal. However, it is only performed after an endoscopy has ruled out structural causes for the symptoms.",
      "Option E: Esophageal manometry is the confirmatory test for motility disorders like achalasia (showing failure of the lower esophageal sphincter to relax) but is not used in the workup of gastroparesis."
