      "Clinical Reasoning: In the absence of beta-glucan, the fungal cell wall becomes osmotic fragile, leading to cell lysis and death. This is particularly effective against Aspergillus and Candida species. In this immunocompromised post-transplant patient, invasive aspergillosis is a life-threatening condition requiring targeted antifungal therapy.",
