      "Option C: This describes the mechanism of azole antifungals (e.g., fluconazole, itraconazole), which inhibit the P450 enzyme 14-alpha-demethylase, preventing the conversion of lanosterol to ergosterol.",
      "Option D: This describes the mechanism of terbinafine, which inhibits squalene epoxidase, leading to an accumulation of toxic squalene and a deficiency in ergosterol synthesis."
