    "question": "A 17-year-old male presents for a sports physical. A systolic murmur is noted at the mid-sternal area, second intercostal space. The murmur does not change with the Valsalva maneuver. He is 6'5\" and weighs 200 lbs. Vitals are within normal limits. What is the most likely explanation for the cardiac finding?",
