    "question": "A 36-year-old female with multiple comorbidities presents with a pseudo-fracture of the left hip after falling from a curb to the ground. She does not drink alcohol or smoke. Serum studies reveal the following: Calcium: 7.2 mg/dL (Normal: 8.4\u201310.2), Phosphorus: 9.0 mg/dL (Normal: 3.0\u20134.5), Creatinine: 3.1 mg/dL (Normal: 0.7\u20131.2), and Alkaline Phosphatase: 400 U/L (Normal: 50\u2013150). Which of the following is the most likely contributory factor to this patient's fracture?",
