      "Option B: LH is elevated in PCOS. Decreased LH and FSH are seen in functional hypothalamic amenorrhea (e.g., anorexia nervosa), where low leptin levels disrupt GnRH pulsation.",
      "Option C: Endometriomas (chocolate cysts) are associated with endometriosis. This condition typically presents with dysmenorrhea (painful periods) and pelvic pain rather than the irregular cycles and androgen excess seen here.",
      "Option D: Prostaglandin (PGF2-alpha) hypersecretion is the primary mechanism for primary dysmenorrhea, which presents as painful menses with a normal physical exam, often in younger women."
