    "question": "A 21-year-old male presents with a one-day history of erythema on his right arm. He works at a fast-food restaurant and burned himself on the forearm three days ago. Physical examination reveals red streaks extending from the burn site towards the axilla. Vitals are within normal limits. What is the most appropriate pharmacologic therapy and diagnosis?",
