    "question": "A 40-year-old male presents with a 2-month history of dry cough and shortness of breath. He has no significant past medical history but has a 5-pack-year smoking history. Chest X-ray reveals cephalization of the pulmonary vessels. A resting echocardiogram shows a left ventricular ejection fraction of 50% (normal: 55-70%). Which of the following is the most likely cause of this patient's clinical findings?",
