      "Option C: Incorrect because ectasia (dilation) and loss of bronchiolar musculature describe bronchiectasis, which presents with chronic, copious, and often foul-smelling sputum production, rather than a dry cough and decreased LVEF.",
      "Option D: Incorrect because an increased Reid index (the ratio of the thickness of the mucous gland layer to the thickness of the wall between the epithelium and cartilage) is characteristic of chronic bronchitis. While chronic bronchitis can lead to cor pulmonale (right heart failure), it does not typically cause a primary decrease in LVEF or cephalization of pulmonary vessels."
