      "Option C: Griseofulvin is a P450 inducer and microtubule inhibitor used primarily for fungal infections like Tinea capitis. As an inducer, it would lower the serum concentration of drugs metabolized by the P450 system.",
      "Option D: Rifampin is a potent P450 inducer used in tuberculosis treatment and for prophylaxis against Neisseria meningitidis. It is known for causing orange-colored bodily secretions (tears, urine).",
      "Option E: St. John's Wort is an herbal supplement for depression that acts as a P450 inducer. It is a common cause of drug-drug interactions and can lead to serotonin syndrome if combined with other serotonergic agents."
