    "question": "A 32-year-old male presents with a two-day history of fever and chills. His temperature is 103\u00b0F (39.4\u00b0C). Physical examination reveals a new murmur consistent with mitral regurgitation. The patient reports undergoing a root canal procedure one week ago. Which of the following characteristics is most likely to be reflective of the most likely causal organism?",
