    "question": "A 64-year-old woman presents with a 5-day history of vaginal bleeding. She reports that her last menstrual period was 14 years ago. Physical examination reveals a 7 cm, freely mobile right adnexal mass. Pelvic ultrasound demonstrates a thickened endometrial stripe and a solid right ovarian mass. An endometrial biopsy is performed, which shows complex hyperplasia. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
