    "question": "A 59-year-old male presents to the emergency department with a 3-week history of dizziness and episodes of near-syncope, particularly when performing yard work or climbing stairs. He has a history of hypertension managed with lisinopril. Physical examination and vital signs are within normal limits. An ECG is performed and shows a PR interval that gradually prolongs until a QRS complex is dropped. What is the most appropriate next step in management?",
