    "question": "A 9-year-old boy presents with a 2-day history of yellow eyes (scleral icterus). He recently recovered from an upper respiratory tract viral infection and did not receive any medications. Laboratory studies show a hemoglobin of 10 g/dL and a total bilirubin of 2 mg/dL. A direct antiglobulin test is positive, and a peripheral blood smear reveals the presence of spherocytes. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
