    "question": "A 34-year-old male on a methadone program is evaluated by a physician for respiratory symptoms. A bronchoalveolar lavage is performed, and a silver stain of the specimen reveals disc-shaped yeast-like cysts. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in pharmacological therapy?",
