    "question": "A 56-year-old male presents with a 1-month history of progressive dry cough and a 6-month history of progressive shortness of breath. Vitals are within normal limits. Auscultation of the chest reveals a loud S2. A CT scan of the chest demonstrates a reticular pattern with honeycombing. Which of the following is the most appropriate pharmacologic therapy for this patient?",
