    "question": "A 49-year-old male hospitalized with multiple comorbidities presents with intractable nosebleeds for the past three days. Laboratory studies show a blood urea nitrogen (BUN) of 120 mg/dL and a serum creatinine of 4.5 mg/dL. A renal biopsy is performed, revealing crescentic glomerulonephritis with fibrin crescents. Which of the following laboratory findings is most likely to be present in this patient?",
