      "Clinical Reasoning: While Cushing disease is often associated with 'buffalo hump' or 'purple striae,' the USMLE may present it more subtly with just weight gain and osteoporosis. In a 45-year-old male, compression fractures are highly unusual and should prompt an investigation into secondary causes of bone loss, such as glucocorticoid excess.",
