    "question": "A 41-year-old woman presents with a dry cough and occasional fevers for the past year. Laboratory studies show a serum calcium of 10.4 mg/dL (normal: 8.4-10.2) and a serum alkaline phosphatase (ALP) of 200 U/L (normal: 50-150). Histological examination of a lung biopsy reveals non-caseating granulomas. Which of the following clinical scenarios is mediated by the same hypersensitivity mechanism as this patient's condition?",
