      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient's presentation of a chronic dry cough, hypercalcemia (caused by 1-alpha-hydroxylase activity in granulomatous macrophages), and elevated ALP (suggesting hepatic or bile ductule involvement) is classic for sarcoidosis. The PPD (purified protein derivative) skin test also relies on Type IV hypersensitivity, where T cells respond to mycobacterial antigens, causing localized induration.",
