      "Clinical Reasoning: Pseudomonas is a common opportunistic pathogen in burn units due to the loss of the primary skin barrier and the moist environment of the wounds. The blue-green color mentioned in the vignette is due to the production of pyocyanin and pyoverdine. Notably, the mechanism of Exotoxin A is identical to that of the Diphtheria toxin produced by Corynebacterium diphtheriae.",
