    "question": "A 9-year-old boy presents with a 2-day history of worsening shortness of breath, dry cough, and fever. He underwent a left renal transplant one year ago for chronic pyelonephritis secondary to recalcitrant vesicoureteral reflux. A lung biopsy is performed and reveals cells with large, dark, intranuclear inclusions surrounded by a clear halo. Which of the following is the most likely causative agent?",
