    "question": "A 9-year-old boy presents with a 3-day history of fever, fatigue, and a persistent cough. He immigrated to the United States from China four years ago. Physical examination reveals a temperature of 101\u00b0F. Laboratory studies show a hemoglobin of 14.5 g/dL, a platelet count of 250,000/mm\u00b3, and a white blood cell count of 40,000/mm\u00b3 with 80% lymphocytes. His blood glucose is 68 mg/dL. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
