    "question": "A 32-year-old female presents with a very tender neck. She reports recently recovering from a viral upper respiratory tract infection. Physical examination is significant for a very tender thyroid gland. Laboratory studies are performed to evaluate her thyroid status. Which of the following combinations of thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH), thyroxine (T4), and radioactive iodine uptake is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
