      "Option B: Anti-dsDNA is specific for Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE). Lupus nephritis (specifically DPGN) can cause hematuria and renal failure, but it lacks the necrotizing upper airway involvement and mononeuritis multiplex seen in this case.",
      "Option C: Anti-GBM antibodies are seen in Goodpasture syndrome. While it causes RPGN (crescents) and pulmonary hemorrhage, it does not involve the upper respiratory tract (sinusitis) or peripheral nerves.",
