      "Clinical Reasoning: The biopsy description of 'large, clear intracytoplasmic vacuoles' is pathognomonic for macrovesicular steatosis. While this can be seen in non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) and Hepatitis C, the patient's history and the AST:ALT ratio of 2:1 strongly point toward alcoholic liver disease.",
