    "question": "A 26-year-old male presents with a 4-day history of foul-smelling stools and bloating. He recently returned from a camping trip where he drank water from a freshwater lake. Light microscopy of a stool sample reveals flagellated, pear-shaped trophozoites and dormant cystic forms. Which of the following is the primary mechanism of action for the first-line treatment of this patient's condition?",
