      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient's presentation of intense pruritus and linear burrows on the hands is pathognomonic for scabies. His social history (living in a group home and recent incarceration) significantly increases the risk of transmission, as scabies spreads easily in crowded living conditions through direct skin-to-skin contact.",
