      "Option B: Dicloxacillin is a penicillinase-resistant penicillin used for staphylococcal skin infections (MSSA) such as cellulitis, impetigo, or mastitis.",
      "Option C: Topical Mupirocin is the treatment of choice for localized impetigo, typically caused by S. aureus or S. pyogenes.",
      "Option E: Triamcinolone is a corticosteroid used for various inflammatory skin conditions (like psoriasis) or as an intra-articular injection for conditions like carpal tunnel syndrome."
