    "question": "A 62-year-old woman presents for follow-up one month after undergoing arteriography through the right leg for evaluation of intermittent claudication. Physical examination reveals a continuous machine-like murmur and a palpable thrill at the arteriography site. There are decreased pedal pulses on the right; however, prior to the procedure, pulses were normal. This patient's acute abnormality can also develop in which of the following unrelated conditions?",
