    "question": "A 41-year-old woman presents with a one-week history of urinary hesitancy and the need to void 10-12 times daily. Physical examination reveals clonus of the left foot and a relative afferent pupillary defect (RAPD) in the right eye. She traveled to Honduras for one week approximately one month ago. Cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) analysis demonstrates the presence of oligoclonal bands. Which of the following is the most appropriate pharmacologic therapy for this patient's current condition?",
