    "question": "A 5-day-old male neonate is brought to the clinic due to bleeding from the umbilical stump. He was born at home via an uncomplicated vaginal delivery. The mother reports that he has been breastfeeding normally and has had no fevers or irritability. Physical examination shows a small amount of fresh blood oozing from the umbilical stump. Small red spots are noted on the conjunctivae bilaterally. The infant is not in acute distress and has a normal pediatric Glasgow Coma Scale score. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
