    "question": "A 24-year-old male presents with a one-month history of a sensation of fullness in his neck. Physical examination reveals a thyroid nodule. Laboratory studies show a TSH level of 2.0 mIU/L (normal range: 0.5\u20135.0 mIU/L). An ultrasound is performed, followed by a fine-needle aspiration (FNA). Histological examination of the FNA sample shows apple-green birefringence under polarized light with Congo red staining. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?",
