      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient's history of extreme prematurity (26 weeks) and long-term oxygen therapy is the classic setup for BPD. The physical findings of right axis deviation (indicating right ventricular hypertrophy) and a loud P2 (indicating pulmonary hypertension) are common sequelae of chronic lung disease in these infants, as chronic hypoxia leads to pulmonary vasoconstriction and remodeling.",
