    "question": "A 71-year-old male with a history of alcoholism, heavy smoking, diabetes, and hypertension, who was previously on dialysis, undergoes an autopsy. Gross examination of the liver reveals multiple, widely distributed lesions throughout the parenchyma. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
