    "question": "A 52-year-old male with a BMI of 35 presents for a routine follow-up. His medical history is significant for type 2 diabetes mellitus and hypertension, for which he takes metformin and lisinopril. He has a 20-pack-year smoking history. Physical examination reveals 3+ pulses in all extremities. The skin on his lower legs appears thickened with a brownish, \"brawny\" discoloration and mild edema. What is the next best step in the diagnosis of this patient's condition?",
