      "Option B: Incorrect because a decreased stool pH is characteristic of lactose intolerance. In lactose intolerance, undigested lactose is fermented by colonic bacteria into short-chain fatty acids and hydrogen gas, lowering the pH. The intestinal villi in lactose intolerance are histologically normal.",
      "Option D: Incorrect because the D-xylose test is used to distinguish between malabsorption caused by mucosal disease versus pancreatic insufficiency. D-xylose is a monosaccharide that requires intact mucosa for absorption but does not require pancreatic enzymes. Therefore, in Celiac disease (mucosal damage), the D-xylose test will be abnormal (low absorption/low urinary excretion). It remains normal in pancreatic insufficiency.",
