    "question": "A 49-year-old woman presents with a 3-month history of worsening pedal edema. She has a long-standing history of rheumatoid arthritis managed with multiple medications. A renal biopsy is performed, and the specimen shows apple-green birefringence under polarized light with Congo Red staining. The molecular pathology responsible for this patient's acute condition is most likely to be seen in a different patient with which of the following clinical findings?",
