      "Clinical Reasoning: The clinical presentation of neonatal meningitis (fever, irritability, poor feeding) combined with the maternal history of consuming deli meats and soft cheeses is classic for Listeria monocytogenes infection. Listeria is one of the top three causes of neonatal meningitis, alongside Group B Streptococcus and E. coli.",
