    "question": "A 54-year-old woman presents with a 1-month history of worsening pedal edema and a 6-month history of mid-to-upper back pain. Laboratory studies show an MCV of 108 fL and a serum calcium of 10.4 mg/dL (normal: 8.4\u201310.2 mg/dL). An X-ray of the humerus reveals multiple lytic lesions. Which of the following is the next best step in diagnosis?",
