    "question": "A 56-year-old woman presents with a one-week history of palpitations. She underwent a mitral valve replacement with a prosthetic valve for rheumatic heart disease three years ago and is currently on warfarin. Physical examination reveals pale conjunctivae. Cardiac examination shows loud systolic and diastolic murmurs. Laboratory studies show a hematocrit of 28%. A blood smear is performed. The findings on the blood smear in this patient are most likely to be seen in which of the following unrelated conditions?",
