      "Clinical Reasoning: The reduction in PaCO2 results in an acute respiratory alkalosis, which manifests as an increased pH. In the acute setting (minutes to hours), the kidneys do not have sufficient time to compensate by excreting bicarbonate; renal compensation typically requires 12 to 24 hours to initiate and days to complete. Therefore, the bicarbonate level remains within the normal range.",
