    "question": "A 9-year-old boy presents with skeletal pain. A skeletal analysis reveals lytic lesions of the skull and ribs. Molecular analysis of the affected tissue shows cells that are CD1a positive, and electron microscopy reveals rod-shaped Birbeck granules. The cell type that is hyperproliferative in this patient's condition is most likely to have which of the following salient functions?",
