    "question": "A 59-year-old male presents with a 6-month history of progressive shortness of breath and a dry cough. He has no significant past medical history and is a non-smoker, though he reports drinking two beers nightly. Physical examination reveals a loud P2 and diffuse dry inspiratory crackles throughout both lung fields. A pulmonary capillary wedge pressure (PCWP) is found to be normal, and the jugular venous pulsation is 3 cm above the costal margin. Which of the following findings is most likely to be seen in this patient?",
