    "question": "A 39-year-old woman presents for a routine follow-up. Physical examination reveals brownish-gold rings around the periphery of the cornea. Slit-lamp examination confirms copper deposition within Descemet's membrane. Genetic testing previously confirmed an autosomal recessive mutation on chromosome 13. Which of the following clinical findings is most likely to be observed in this patient?",
