      "Clinical Reasoning: In sensorineural hearing loss, the Rinne test remains 'normal' or positive (Air Conduction > Bone Conduction) because the external and middle ear structures are intact; however, the overall perception of sound is diminished. The Weber test, which involves placing a tuning fork on the midline of the skull, will lateralize to the contralateral (healthy) ear because the affected ear has a neural deficit and cannot process the vibrations as effectively as the healthy side.",
      "Key Association: For a left-sided lesion causing SNHL, the Weber test lateralizes to the right (the 'better' ear)."
