      "Clinical Reasoning: Adequate basal levels of leptin are required for the normal pulsatile release of Gonadotropin-Releasing Hormone (GnRH) from the hypothalamus. When leptin is low, GnRH pulsatility is suppressed (hypogonadotropic hypogonadism). This leads to decreased secretion of LH and FSH from the anterior pituitary. Without the appropriate LH surge, ovulation does not occur. The absence of ovulation means no corpus luteum is formed, resulting in low levels of luteal progesterone.",
