      "Primary Mechanism: Granulosa cell tumors are the most common sex cord-stromal tumors and are known for secreting estrogen. In a postmenopausal woman, this excess estrogen leads to unopposed stimulation of the endometrial lining, which manifests as endometrial hyperplasia and subsequent vaginal bleeding.",
