      "Option D: Mucinous cystadenocarcinoma is an epithelial ovarian tumor that can lead to pseudomyxoma peritonei (mucin accumulation in the peritoneal cavity) but does not cause endometrial hyperplasia.",
      "Option E: Sertoli-Leydig cell tumors typically secrete androgens, leading to virilization (hirsutism, voice deepening) in females. While they can cause gynecomastia in males via aromatization, they are not the primary cause of endometrial hyperplasia in this context."
