    "question": "An 8-year-old boy presents with a 2-day history of swelling of the left eye. He recently recovered from an upper respiratory tract infection. Physical examination reveals a temperature of 102\u00b0F, erythema, and edema of the periorbital tissues. The patient has significant difficulty opening the left eye due to the swelling. Further examination shows restricted extraocular movements (ophthalmoplegia) and protrusion of the globe (proptosis). Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
