      "Primary Mechanism: Necrotizing enterocolitis (NEC) is a life-threatening condition primarily affecting premature infants. The pathophysiology involves a combination of intestinal immaturity, mucosal injury, and bacterial colonization, leading to inflammation and necrosis of the bowel wall. Pneumatosis intestinalis, the presence of gas within the intestinal wall, is a pathognomonic radiographic finding.",
