    "question": "A 17-year-old boy presents with a 3-month history of intermittent blood in his stool. His past medical history is unremarkable, and he reports no recent travel. Physical examination is normal, and vitals are within normal limits. A biopsy of the intestinal mucosa is performed, and histopathology reveals the presence of non-caseating granulomas composed of activated macrophages fused into multinucleated giant cells. Which of the following conditions is this patient most likely to develop in the future?",
