    "question": "A 31-year-old male presents with a 2-day history of sharp left-sided chest pain that worsens with coughing or deep inspiration. Four days ago, he recovered from a short illness characterized by coryza and a low-grade fever. Physical examination reveals a left-sided friction rub, while the cardiac examination is normal. A chest X-ray shows a small pleural effusion on the left side. Serum creatine kinase (CK) levels are within the normal range. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
