    "question": "A 24-year-old female at 40 weeks gestation is in labor. Fetal heart rate monitoring is performed during parturition. The tracing reveals a symmetric decrease in the fetal heart rate that begins at the onset of a uterine contraction and returns to baseline at the conclusion of the contraction. The nadir of the heart rate dip occurs simultaneously with the peak of the uterine contraction. Which of the following is the most likely cause of this finding?",
