    "question": "A 64-year-old woman with a history of type 2 diabetes and hypertension presents for a routine follow-up. Her current medications include metformin and lisinopril. Physical examination is unremarkable. Laboratory studies show a serum creatinine of 1.2 mg/dL and urinary protein of 1+. A graph of her parathyroid hormone (PTH) and serum calcium levels shows a data point within the normal range for both parameters. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
