    "question": "A 17-year-old boy presents with a 2-day history of fatigue, fever, and a non-productive cough. He is febrile at 101\u00b0F. Physical examination reveals pale conjunctivae. A chest X-ray shows bilateral interstitial infiltrates. A sample of blood drawn for testing agglutinates spontaneously while being transported to the laboratory. Which of the following is the most likely causative organism?",
