    "question": "A 66-year-old woman is evaluated in the hospital. Laboratory studies are performed, and a diagram is used to plot her results with parathyroid hormone (PTH) levels on the y-axis and serum calcium levels on the x-axis. A data point (magenta dot) indicates that the patient has significantly elevated serum calcium and suppressed PTH levels. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
