    "question": "A 7-year-old girl is brought in for a cardiopulmonary examination. A schematic of her heart and associated vessels shows the following oxygen tension (PO2) percentages: Vena Cava (73%), Right Atrium (73%), Right Ventricle (73%), Pulmonary Artery (73%), Left Atrium (96%), and Left Ventricle (85%). Which of the following is the most likely defect?",
