    "question": "A 54-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain for the past 2 hours. She has a medical history of polycythemia vera. Physical examination reveals mild scleral icterus. Abdominal examination shows a fluid wave and a moderately large liver and spleen. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
