    "question": "A 24-year-old woman presents with a ruptured appendix and sepsis. Her blood pressure is stable. An exploratory laparoscopy is performed, revealing a collection of pus. A Gram stain of the pus shows neutrophils, gram-positive rods and cocci, and gram-negative rods. An aerobic culture on MacConkey agar yields Enterococci. Which of the following bacteria is most likely to be among the gram-negative rods seen on the initial Gram stain?",
