      "Option C: Legionella pneumophila is a gram-negative rod typically associated with atypical pneumonia, often linked to contaminated water sources like air conditioning systems; it would not be a primary suspect in a ruptured appendix.",
      "Option D: Moraxella catarrhalis is a gram-negative diplococcus (not a rod) that is a common cause of otitis media and respiratory infections, not intra-abdominal abscesses.",
      "Option E: Proteus mirabilis is a gram-negative rod associated with urinary tract infections and the formation of staghorn (struvite) calculi due to its urease-positive nature; it would typically grow on aerobic cultures."
