    "question": "A 7-year-old girl is brought in for a routine cardiopulmonary examination. A schematic of oxygen tension (PO2) in various heart chambers and vessels is obtained: Vena Cava (73%), Right Atrium (73%), Right Ventricle (73%), Pulmonary Artery (73%), Left Atrium (96%), and Left Ventricle (85%). Which of the following is the most likely defect?",
