    "question": "A 39-year-old woman with a 10-year history of rheumatoid arthritis presents for a follow-up. She is currently managed with multiple medications. Pulmonary function testing reveals a normal FEV1/FVC ratio. A chest X-ray shows mild reticulonodularity bilaterally. An agent that inhibits which of the following is the most likely explanation for the patient's presentation?",
