      "Option B: Cyclooxygenase (COX) inhibitors include NSAIDs and acetaminophen. NSAIDs are associated with GI bleeding and renal insufficiency, while acetaminophen toxicity leads to hepatic failure via the NAPQI metabolite.",
      "Option D: Glucocorticoids decrease the signaling of the NF-kappaB pathway. Normally, I-kappaB binds and sequesters NF-kappaB in the cytosol; steroids prevent the phosphorylation of I-kappaB, thereby preventing the release of NF-kappaB to the nucleus where it would otherwise upregulate pro-inflammatory genes.",
