    "learning_objective": "The Bottom Line: Methotrexate, a dihydrofolate reductase inhibitor used as a first-line DMARD for rheumatoid arthritis, is associated with adverse effects including pulmonary fibrosis (reticulonodular pattern on CXR), agranulocytosis, and hepatotoxicity.",
