    "question": "A 49-year-old male is brought to the emergency department by his wife 30 minutes after the abrupt onset of severe abdominal pain. He describes the pain as feeling like he was \"kicked in the abdomen.\" He has a history of abdominal pain after meals, for which he frequently takes over-the-counter antacids. Physical examination reveals a rigid abdomen with guarding. An upright chest X-ray is performed and shows a thin crescent of lucency beneath the right hemidiaphragm. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
