      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient's history of postprandial abdominal pain relieved by antacids is highly suggestive of chronic peptic ulcer disease. The sudden, excruciating \"kicked in the abdomen\" pain indicates an acute perforation. The chest X-ray finding of air under the diaphragm (pneumoperitoneum) confirms the diagnosis of a perforated viscus, requiring emergent surgical consultation.",
