    "question": "A 6-year-old girl presents with a one-day history of a painful left hip. She recently recovered from an upper respiratory viral infection. Physical examination shows no redness or swelling of the hip, and she is able to bear weight. Laboratory studies show a leukocyte count of 10,000/\u00b5L (normal range 4,000-11,000). Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
