    "question": "A 47-year-old woman presents with a 3-week history of gradual onset back pain. She has no history of trauma and is a non-smoker and non-drinker. Laboratory studies, including urinalysis, are within normal limits. An X-ray of the spine reveals two lytic lesions at the T8 and T9 vertebrae. Which of the following is the most likely explanation for these findings?",
