    "question": "A 29-year-old woman presents with a 1-week history of red discoloration on her fingers. She also reports a 3-month history of progressive daytime fatigue. She has a history of recurrent nosebleeds since adolescence. She works as a dental hygienist and has no family history of autoimmune disease. Physical examination reveals several small, non-blanching red macules on her fingertips and tongue. Which of the following is the most likely underlying mechanism for her condition?",
