    "question": "A 33-year-old woman presents with a one-week history of an unpredictable urge to void, necessitating 8 to 12 trips to the bathroom daily. She also reports blurry vision in her left eye. Physical examination reveals decreased visual acuity in the left eye, mild spasticity in both arms, and clonus of the left foot. An MRI of the brain demonstrates multiple periventricular white matter plaques. Intravenous corticosteroid therapy is initiated. Following resolution of the acute symptoms, which of the following agents is most likely to decrease the recurrence of this patient's symptoms?",
