    "question": "A 65-year-old male presents with a persistent fever following a bowel resection for complicated diverticulitis. He has been on broad-spectrum antibiotics for the past three weeks since the operation. Physical examination reveals a central venous catheter that was placed on the day of surgery. Cultures from the tip of the catheter grown on sheep blood agar show purple budding organisms. Which of the following is the most likely causal organism?",
