    "question": "A 71-year-old male presents with a 3-week history of a diffuse red rash over most of his body. Physical examination reveals diffuse erythroderma, but the palms and soles are notably spared. A peripheral blood smear is performed and shows T lymphocytes with characteristic cerebriform nuclei. The viral etiology most commonly associated with this condition typically possesses which of the following genomic and structural characteristics?",
