      "Option C: Herpes simplex virus (HHV-1 and HHV-2) are DNA viruses that cause localized vesicular lesions (oral or genital) and, while they can disseminate in the immunocompromised, VZV is the classic cause of a generalized vesicular rash with pneumonia.",
      "Option D: Rubella virus is a positive-sense, single-stranded RNA virus (Togavirus) that typically presents with a maculopapular rash and lymphadenopathy, not a vesicular rash and nodular pneumonia."
