    "question": "A 32-year-old male presents to the physician with general malaise, a rash, and blood in his urine. He recently started a course of antibiotics for a skin infection four days ago. Urinalysis reveals 3+ blood, 1+ protein, and 120 leukocytes per high-power field, of which 25% are eosinophils. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
