    "incorrect_explanations": [
      "Option B: Decreased cAMP is typically associated with Gi-protein coupled receptor activation, which would generally oppose relaxation or promote contraction.",
      "Option C: Increased IP3 (Inositol trisphosphate) is the result of Gq-protein coupled receptor activation. This pathway increases intracellular calcium, which activates MLCK and leads to smooth muscle contraction, the opposite of the effect seen at point X.",
      "Option D: Decreased IP3 is not the primary mechanism by which PGE2 analogs induce smooth muscle relaxation in the context of cervical ripening.",
      "Option E: Phospholipase A2 is the enzyme responsible for releasing arachidonic acid from the cell membrane, which is the precursor for all prostaglandins. While part of the endogenous pathway, it is not the mechanism of action for an exogenous PGE2 analog like dinoprostone.",
      "Option F: Decreased phospholipase A2 activity is the primary mechanism of action for corticosteroids, which inhibit the production of inflammatory mediators."
    ],
    "learning_objective": "The Bottom Line: Dinoprostone is a Prostaglandin E2 (PGE2) analog that induces smooth muscle relaxation and cervical ripening by increasing intracellular cAMP, leading to the inactivation of myosin light chain kinase.",
