    "question": "A 27-year-old G0P0 woman presents to the physician with a 3-day history of pain in her right breast. Physical examination reveals a red, warm, tender, non-fluctuant mass in the right outer quadrant. Her temperature is 101.3\u00b0F. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
