      "Clinical Reasoning: The patient presents with classic signs of inflammation (red, warm, tender mass) and systemic involvement (fever of 101.3\u00b0F). The critical clinical differentiator in this vignette is the description of the mass as 'non-fluctuant.' Fluctuance indicates a localized collection of fluid (pus), which would point toward an abscess. A solid, tender, inflamed area without fluctuance is diagnostic of mastitis.",
