    "question": "A 55-year-old woman presents to the physician for a three-month history of fatigue and diffuse itching. She has no history of abdominal pain. Physical examination reveals jaundice and a palpable, non-tender epigastric mass. Her hands show tar-stained fingers. Laboratory studies show an alkaline phosphatase of 300 IU/L, total bilirubin of 4.0 mg/dL, and serum amylase of 40 U/L. Which of the following is the next best step in diagnosis?",
