    "question": "A 16-year-old boy is brought to the clinic by his mother for a 6-week history of unusual behavior. She reports that he has been mumbling to himself and appears to be responding to internal stimuli. He is diagnosed with a psychiatric condition and prescribed an antipsychotic medication. Four hours after the first dose, he returns to the clinic with a crooked neck (torticollis). A second pharmacological agent is administered to treat this side effect. Which of the following best describes the molecular effect of this second agent?",
    "vitals": null,
