    "question": "A 42-year-old woman with systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) is brought to the emergency department by her husband after an apparent seizure. Her Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) is 15. A CT scan of the head reveals a ring-enhancing lesion. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
